                                                "sense_id": "3081a7fa-e55a-3cf2-a39b-bbba41cc18ea",
                                                "text": "Butters such as cocoa, illippe, kokum, mango, murumuru, sal (shorea) and shea occur naturally and are obtained directly from the plant."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "015b4338-1814-4ca8-90f0-20143078ca0b",
                                                "sense_id": "3081a7fa-e55a-3cf2-a39b-bbba41cc18ea",
                                                "text": "Butters are triglycerides […]. Cocoa butter (Theobroma cacao) is used as an emollient in topical cosmetic formulations, […] South American and the Brazilian rainforest offer various plants with common butters used in the industry that include […] cupuaçu butter […] and murumuru butter from the murumuru palm tree (Astrocaryum murumuru). India is another source of many butters used in cosmetic products, including kokum butter extracted from the seeds of the Garcinia indica tree, mango butter from the Mangifera indica tree and shea butter[…]"
                                            }
